 @CleonofAthens  Yeah m8 I can tell you that you are not alone. I understand how infuriating it must be having those issues - especially when someone else with your exact setup can have 0 issues and everything just runs fine - so finding a fix is freaking impossible - and not even Intel knows what the hell is going wrong.

So in that - I would - if I were you - sell the Arc and get whatever you can get for it - and then get something like an RX 6650 XT for 240$ or maybe this RX 7600 for 270$. I know it's not optimal and will most likely cost you like 100$ or something like that more than what you can get for your Arc card - however it will fix your issues I'm sure (Never seen a single issue with the RX 6600, RX 6600 XT or RX 6650 XT - and I've seen A LOT of them)

And I must admit that I'm looking at that whole "8GB is not enough" thing - and not seeing any of that in any game in 1080p. The max you will ever need to do at 1080p with 8GB is to turn off some "special" thing a game for some reason has in it which uses up a lot of memory... however seeing how my wifes PC + our guest PC is running with an RX 6650 XT - and I've LITERALLY tested every "demanding" game on Gamepass and a bunch on steam as well -  I can tell you that I have yet to see ANY kind of "dropped ball" from the RX 6650 XT in ANY game at 1080p... I'm wondering what the hell that whole "8GB is not enough even for 1080p" is all about... I'm thinking everyone saying it is just flatout wrong - even at 1440p I find it a bit dubious. I feel a bit like some people have forgotten what "mid range" actually means 😀Mid range is supposed to have "enough" for a good gaming experience and might involve a bit of tweaking the settings - and no more than that. 16GB seems like a massive overkill for anything less than a 6800 XT or a 4070... But hey that's just me - I will probably trigger someone by saying that - but I'm just speaking from my experiences servicing gaming PCs for my entire friends and family sphere - so - I only see about 40 PCs regularly because I stopped doing it for a job 😀I might be missing something but - every time someone brings it up it has a distinct lack of "evidence" to follow it.
